{"id": "spam_sa::sa::easy_ham::0526.615f918b4860d437577f6aa66c9b37cf", "subject": "Re: Selling Wedded Bliss (was Re: Ouch...)", "body": "Turpin:\n>>Do we have any statistics on the poor man's divorce from centuries past?\n\nEugen Leitl:\n>That's easy. Divorce didn't happen.\n\nYou seem not to know what a \"poor man's divorce\" is.\nIt is an old term, from the time when divorce was\ndifficult, but walking was easy, and identity was\nnot so locked down as it is today. Not every widow\nhad a dead husband.\n\n>I'm seeing lack of innovation ..\n\nThat doesn't tell us anything except what is\nhappening in Eugen Leitl's life. The more common\nobservation is that the rate of change is increasing.\nDo you have any data that might persuade us that what\nyou see is more telling than what others see?\n\n>gerontocracy favors gerontocracy.\n\nI would have thought that gerontocracy favors biotech\nresearch and plenty of young workers to pay taxes.\nNote that the fertility rate doesn't result from\ndecisions made by the old, but by the young. If we\nwant more kids, we have to convince people who are\nin their twenties to become parents.\n\n\n\n\n_________________________________________________________________\nJoin the world�s largest e-mail service with MSN Hotmail. \nhttp://www.hotmail.com", "from": "Russell Turpin <deafbox@hotmail.com>", "attachments": [], "label": "ham"}
{"id": "trec06c_zip::data/normal/4618", "subject": "● Siemens Internship Opportunity", "body": "Position Description:\nResearch Intern for Software Testing Quality &amp; Process Modeling\nThe position will involve in the research project of measuring quality of testing, which is jointly sponsored by Siemens Corporate Technology and COM MN. This study aims to provide advanced tools and technologies to support testing management and improve testing quality.\nThe successful completion of this project would lead to new views in software reliability engineering under Siemens environment. The first phase of the project mainly focuses on design and implementation of an innovative model used to predict residual defects and estimate the quality of system testing. \n \nRequirements:\n&amp;#8226;         Ph.D or M.S candidate in computer science.\n&amp;#8226;         Good English reading and writing skills.\n&amp;#8226;         Proficiency in at least one programming language (C/C++/Java)\n&amp;#8226;         Good understanding of software development process (e.g. CMM)\n&amp;#8226;         Experienced in conducting statistical analysis via mathematic / statistical tools (MatLab, MathCad, Mathematica, etc).\n&amp;#8226;         Experience and knowledge in mobile communication network is highly desirable.\n&amp;#8226;         Knowledge and experience in Excel VBA programming is highly desirable.\nAbility to work independently on the programming assignment, while interacting with the other researchers on design and experimentation.\nSend you resume to: internship.cn@siemens.com    before August\n\n", "from": "Tran Quang Anh <mei@cernet.edu.cn>", "attachments": [], "label": "ham"}
